.TH KEYWAVE.CONF 5 "March 2026" "Keywave Manual" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
keywave.conf \- Configuration file format for Keywave
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/keywave/keywave.conf\fR
.br
\fI~/.config/keywave/keywave.conf\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBkeywave.conf\fR file configures the runtime behavior of the
.BR keywave (1)
daemon. The file uses a standard key-value format. Lines beginning with \fB#\fR or \fB;\fR
are treated as comments and ignored. Section headers in brackets (e.g. \fB[keywave]\fR) are optional and ignored.
.SH DIRECTIVES
.TP
.BI volume " = float"
Sets the playback master volume. Must be a non-negative floating-point number (e.g. \fB0.8\fR, \fB1.0\fR).
Default is \fB1.0\fR.
.TP
.BI keyboard_volume " = float"
.TQ
.BI keyboard_vol " = float"
Sets the volume override specifically for keyboard audio playback.
.TP
.BI mouse_volume " = float"
.TQ
.BI mouse_vol " = float"
Sets the volume override specifically for mouse click audio playback.
.TP
.BI keyboard_pack " = path"
.TQ
.BI keyboard_soundpack " = path"
.TQ
.BI soundpack " = path"
Specifies the filesystem path to a Mechvibes/Wayvibes-compatible keyboard soundpack directory containing a \fBconfig.json\fR file.
Tilde (\fB~\fR) expansion to the user's home directory is supported.
.TP
.BI mouse_sound " = path"
.TQ
.BI mouse_soundpack " = path"
.TQ
.BI mouse " = path"
Specifies the filesystem path to an audio file (e.g., WAV, MP3, FLAC) to play when mouse click events occur.
Tilde (\fB~\fR) expansion to the user's home directory is supported.
.TP
.BI keyboard_device " = name|path"
.TQ
.BI keyboard_dev " = name|path"
Specifies the keyboard device name (case-insensitive substring match) or explicit filesystem path. If omitted, Keywave automatically detects the keyboard.
.TP
.BI mouse_device " = name|path"
.TQ
.BI mouse_dev " = name|path"
Specifies the mouse device name (case-insensitive substring match) or explicit filesystem path. If omitted, Keywave automatically detects the mouse.
.SH EXAMPLES
A typical \fBkeywave.conf\fR file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Keywave configuration example
volume = 0.75
keyboard_pack = ~/.local/share/keywave/soundpacks/cherrymx-red-abs
mouse_sound = ~/.local/share/keywave/soundpacks/mouse-click.mp3

# Optional explicit device selection by name (run 'keywave -l' to see names)
keyboard_device = ITE Tech. Inc. ITE Device(8176) Keyboard
mouse_device = Logitech M585/M590
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR keywave (1)
